WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.840
It's time to dust off the&nbsp;
fedora and crack the whip one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:07.680
more time! As our favorite globetrotting&nbsp;
archaeologist returns to the big screen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:12.844
here's everything you need to know about&nbsp;
Indiana Jones and the Dial of Destiny.

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:16.740
The last time we saw Indiana Jones, he was&nbsp;
exploring the jungles of South America,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:21.900
avoiding killer ants, and hanging out with&nbsp;
a greaser sidekick played by Shia LaBeouf.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:27.060
Kingdom of the Crystal Skull hit theaters all the&nbsp;
way back in 2008, and it was actually the second&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:32.760
highest-grossing film of that year worldwide, but&nbsp;
it's not exactly beloved by hardcore Indy fans.

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:35.520
So the stakes are pretty high for Dial of Destiny,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:40.200
which is set to land in theaters a little&nbsp;
over 15 years after the last adventure. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:44.760
was originally supposed to be released in&nbsp;
July 2019, but two additional release date&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:50.760
changes and one pandemic later, it's finally&nbsp;
scheduled to hit theaters on June 30, 2023.

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:56.100
Indiana Jones has faced his fair share of&nbsp;
bad guys over the years. In Crystal Skull,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:58.620
he was up against a group&nbsp;
of Soviets in South America,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:03.420
and he narrowly avoided having a heart to&nbsp;
heart with a cult leader in Temple of Doom.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:08.820
But there's one particular group of baddies&nbsp;
who cross Indy's path again and again: Nazis.

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:14.040
As it turns out, Indy's not done with the Third&nbsp;
Reich just yet, as he'll be butting heads with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:18.540
some sinister Nazi faithful in The Dial of&nbsp;
Destiny. According to an exclusive report&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:24.360
from Empire Magazine, the film will be set in&nbsp;
1969 during the height of the Space Race. In&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:28.620
both the film and in real life, the American&nbsp;
government employed multiple Nazi scientists&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:34.320
to beat the Russians to the moon. In Dial of&nbsp;
Destiny, one of them is the nefarious Voller,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:39.600
whose loyalty to Hitler's regime remains strong.&nbsp;
According to Mads Mikkelsen, who plays Voller,

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:43.620
"He's a man who would like to correct some of&nbsp;
the mistakes of the past. There is something&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:47.460
that could make the world a much better place to&nbsp;
live in. He would love to get his hands on it."

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:53.040
We're assuming that that something is the Dial of&nbsp;
Destiny, which Indy will need to find first with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:57.840
the help of his goddaughter Helena. The story&nbsp;
will also focus on Indy truly growing old and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:02.760
getting ready to take off his fedora for good. As&nbsp;
writer-director James Mangold explained to Empire,

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:07.740
"It became really important to me to figure out&nbsp;
how to make this a movie about a hero at sunset."

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:10.140
We'll also get some clarification on what's going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.140 --> 00:02:13.680
on with Shia LaBeouf's Mutt Williams.&nbsp;
While the actor won't appear in the film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:18.578
Mangold told Entertainment Weekly that&nbsp;
we'll indeed learn what happened to him.

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:22.800
You simply can't think of Harrison Ford&nbsp;
without also thinking of Indiana Jones,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:28.500
and vice versa. And Ford seems to genuinely love&nbsp;
playing Indy. So even though he's 80 years old,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:32.665
he'll be stepping onto screens for&nbsp;
one more go-round as Dr. Jones.

00:02:32.665 --> 00:02:37.140
"I'd always wanted to see Indiana&nbsp;
Jones at the end of his career,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.140 --> 00:02:40.320
towards the end of his life, when&nbsp;
everything catches up to him."

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:45.420
John Rhys-Davies will also be returning to&nbsp;
play Indy's best friend Sallah. Outside of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:49.740
this franchise, Rhys-Davies is probably&nbsp;
best known as the ax-wielding dwarf Gimli&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.740 --> 00:02:53.520
in the Lord of the Rings. Indy will also&nbsp;
be teaming up with a new character in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:57.780
form of his goddaughter Helena, whom James&nbsp;
Mangold described to Empire as "slippery,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.780 --> 00:03:02.520
charming, the girl next door" and "a grifter."&nbsp;
She'll be played by Phoebe Waller-Bridge,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.520 --> 00:03:05.760
who's best known as the creator&nbsp;
and star of the sitcom Fleabag.

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:11.040
As for the big bad, it'll be Mads Mikkelsen as&nbsp;
Nazi scientist Voller, who's tricked the U.S.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:15.360
government into thinking he's abandoned his&nbsp;
old ways. Mikkelsen is no stranger to playing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:20.640
antagonists, as he's delivered villainous turns&nbsp;
in the likes of Casino Royale, Fantastic Beasts:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:25.860
The Secrets of Dumbledore, Doctor Strange,&nbsp;
and as the title cannibal on NBC's Hannibal.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.860 --> 00:03:31.800
Voller's murderous enforcer Klaber will be played&nbsp;
by Boyd Holbrook, another actor who specializes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:36.780
in scary roles, like Commander Donald Pierce&nbsp;
in Logan and the Corinthian in The Sandman.

00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:42.000
In addition to those big names, Antonio Banderas&nbsp;
is set to show up in a cameo role. Plus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:46.680
Toby Jones will play Helena's dad Basil.&nbsp;
The cast will be rounded out by Shaunette&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:51.419
Renée Wilson, Thomas Kretschmann,&nbsp;
and bodybuilder Olivier Richters.

00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:55.680
When you think of the behind-the-scenes&nbsp;
talent of Indiana Jones, obviously Steven&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.680 --> 00:04:00.300
Spielberg springs to mind. The celebrated&nbsp;
filmmaker directed the first four Indy films,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:04.140
and it's almost impossible to imagine the&nbsp;
franchise moving on without him. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:09.300
Dial of Destiny won't see Spielberg calling the&nbsp;
shots. While he will remain on hand as a producer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.300 --> 00:04:13.200
he stepped away from the director's chair so&nbsp;
that a younger filmmaker could take the reins.

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:17.940
That leaves The Dial of Destiny in the very&nbsp;
capable hands of James Mangold, who should be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:22.920
a great fit. The story is supposedly about an&nbsp;
aging Indy going on one last adventure before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.920 --> 00:04:28.200
riding off into the sunset, and Mangold has some&nbsp;
promising experience in that area. He co-wrote and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:33.960
directed 2017's Logan, which is the acclaimed swan&nbsp;
song to 20th Century Fox's version of Wolverine.

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:36.600
"Look. I gotta go."

00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:41.520
In addition to Logan, Mangold's credits&nbsp;
include the Western 3:10 to Yuma, the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.520 --> 00:04:48.000
crime drama Cop Land, the Johnny Cash biopic Walk&nbsp;
the Line, and the sports drama Ford v Ferrari.

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:52.920
When it comes to film composers, there's&nbsp;
none more famous than John Williams. Jaws,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.920 --> 00:04:57.600
Jurassic Park, Star Wars, E.T., Harry&nbsp;
Potter, and Superman are just a sampling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.600 --> 00:05:01.020
of his iconic pieces. He even came&nbsp;
up with the theme for the Olympics.

00:05:01.020 --> 00:05:06.180
Williams is also responsible for the rousing&nbsp;
scores that accompany Indiana Jones on each of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:10.380
his adventures. And he'll be back for Dial&nbsp;
of Destiny, providing music that's sure to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.380 --> 00:05:15.180
get the blood pumping as Indy traverses the globe&nbsp;
once again. Interestingly, at one point in time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.180 --> 00:05:19.620
Williams implied that The Fabelmans and&nbsp;
Dial of Destiny would be his last projects&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.620 --> 00:05:24.600
before retiring. However, in January 2023, he&nbsp;
walked those statements back, as he explained,

00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:30.000
"I'll stick around for a while. I can't retire&nbsp;
from music. A day without music is a mistake."

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:35.100
The teaser for Indiana Jones and the&nbsp;
Dial of Destiny dropped in December 2022&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:39.360
and promised all sorts of adventures for&nbsp;
our aging hero. When the preview starts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:42.780
it seems that Indy has been living&nbsp;
the quiet life of a college professor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:47.160
as an exchange between him and Sallah&nbsp;
makes clear. His old friend laments&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.160 --> 00:05:52.178
that he misses waking up in anticipation of the&nbsp;
exciting adventures promised by each new day.

00:05:52.178 --> 00:05:54.360
"Those days have come and gone."

00:05:54.360 --> 00:05:57.120
"Perhaps. Perhaps not."

00:05:57.120 --> 00:06:02.340
But while Dr. Jones may be done with adventure,&nbsp;
adventure isn't quite done with Dr. Jones. As&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:06.600
the teaser progresses, we see Indy picking up&nbsp;
his whip, getting in a showdown atop a train,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.600 --> 00:06:10.500
and exploring ruins filled with Greek&nbsp;
statues. He also makes his way through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.500 --> 00:06:14.700
a Nazi castle and an exciting chase at&nbsp;
a ticker-tape parade for the Apollo 11&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.700 --> 00:06:19.260
astronauts. The whole time, he regales us&nbsp;
with his unique worldview, as he declares,

00:06:19.260 --> 00:06:24.338
"I don't believe in magic, but a few times in my&nbsp;
life, I've seen things, things I can't explain."

00:06:24.338 --> 00:06:29.419
"And I've come to believe it's not so much what&nbsp;
you believe, it's how hard you believe it."

00:06:29.419 --> 00:06:35.100
In April 2023, we were finally treated to the full&nbsp;
official trailer, which is scored to the classic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.100 --> 00:06:40.380
Rolling Stones song "Sympathy for the Devil." That&nbsp;
tune makes it clear that Indy is a man outside of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.380 --> 00:06:45.420
time in the strange world of the 1960s. Speaking&nbsp;
of time, it's possible that that theme might play&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:50.160
a big part in the film, as Voller explains why&nbsp;
he wants to get his hands on the Dial of Destiny.

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:54.060
"Hitler made mistakes, and with&nbsp;
this, I will correct them all."

00:06:54.060 --> 00:06:59.160
Could time travel somehow factor into all of this?&nbsp;
Is that why so many people want the Dial? Not only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.160 --> 00:07:04.140
are the Nazis after it, not only is Indy trying&nbsp;
to get it, but it also looks like Helena has an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.140 --> 00:07:09.420
agenda of her own, as she too is trying to get&nbsp;
her hands on this precious artifact. This prompts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.420 --> 00:07:14.160
a three-way chase across the world, complete&nbsp;
with undersea exploration and aerial action,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:18.000
all in the pursuit of something that could&nbsp;
very well change the course of history.

00:07:18.364 --> 00:07:24.120
Harrison Ford is obviously a Hollywood legend,&nbsp;
but he's also still just a mortal who ages like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.120 --> 00:07:28.020
everyone else. He's 80 years old, and&nbsp;
he presumably can't run around beating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.020 --> 00:07:32.160
up Nazis forever. Plenty of us thought that&nbsp;
he would hang up the fedora for good after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.160 --> 00:07:36.120
Kingdom of the Crystal Skull. But here&nbsp;
he goes again, in what surely must be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.120 --> 00:07:40.680
the final adventure. In an interview with&nbsp;
Total Film in April 2023, Ford revealed,

00:07:40.680 --> 00:07:44.400
"This is the final film in the series,&nbsp;
and this is the last time I'll play the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:48.426
character. I anticipate that it will be&nbsp;
the last time that he appears in a film."

00:07:48.426 --> 00:07:49.702
"For me, this is it."

00:07:49.702 --> 00:07:55.230
"Harrison, let me tell you something. You've&nbsp;
told me that two Indiana Joneses ago."

00:07:55.230 --> 00:07:59.520
Granted, that claim may be a little naive&nbsp;
on Ford's part. If Hollywood can find a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.520 --> 00:08:03.480
way to reboot this franchise or start&nbsp;
a prequel series, they will. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.480 --> 00:08:08.940
we do believe Ford when he says that this&nbsp;
is the last time he'll play Indy. And if it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.940 --> 00:08:13.309
sounds like we're crying, that's just the dust&nbsp;
from all those ancient artifacts in our eyes.

00:08:13.500 --> 00:08:18.120
De-aging technology is a great tool, but&nbsp;
its uses in film thus far have been a bit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.120 --> 00:08:22.320
wonky. The Irishman, for example, is a&nbsp;
fantastic movie, with a terrific Robert&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.320 --> 00:08:26.580
De Niro performance. But those scenes with&nbsp;
him as a younger man just look plain weird.

00:08:26.580 --> 00:08:31.560
However, it sounds like Dial of Destiny is&nbsp;
taking de-aging technology to the next level.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.560 --> 00:08:36.240
While most of the movie will be set during the&nbsp;
late 60s, the opening act will take place during&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.240 --> 00:08:41.700
World War II. This segment will reportedly run&nbsp;
for 25 minutes, which means that James Mangold&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.700 --> 00:08:45.840
must have plenty of faith in the de-aging&nbsp;
tech if we're going to be looking at an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.840 --> 00:08:50.760
artificially youthful Harrison Ford for nearly&nbsp;
half an hour. As Mangold gushed to Total Film,

00:08:50.760 --> 00:08:53.520
"It was an incredible technology&nbsp;
[...] The goal was to give the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.520 --> 00:08:56.220
audience a full-bodied taste&nbsp;
of what they missed so much."

00:08:56.220 --> 00:09:01.380
From the clips we've seen of the opening sequence,&nbsp;
Ford looks pretty fantastic, and better even than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.380 --> 00:09:06.600
recent examples of de-aging like Sean Young in&nbsp;
Blade Runner 2049 or Kurt Russell in Guardians&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.600 --> 00:09:11.400
of the Galaxy Vol. 2. Evidently,&nbsp;
the jump from the 40s to the 60s is going to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.400 --> 00:09:15.780
key to the story in Dial of Destiny. The film&nbsp;
will be hopping from an era when it was clear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.780 --> 00:09:20.520
who the bad guys were to a much more complicated&nbsp;
time. As Mangold told The Hollywood Reporter,

00:09:20.520 --> 00:09:24.360
"It's not just a movie about a hero in&nbsp;
his twilight years who is called back into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.360 --> 00:09:28.800
action. It's more than just that his bones&nbsp;
might ache, it's that his soul might ache,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.800 --> 00:09:32.760
or that some of his optimism or sense [of]&nbsp;
fitting into the world might have evaporated."

00:09:32.760 --> 00:09:37.260
Furthermore, Indy will be dealing with a body&nbsp;
that's much older and creakier than before.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.260 --> 00:09:42.720
Slugging bad guys in the face isn't going to be&nbsp;
as easy as it once was, with Mangold explaining,

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:48.060
"It reminds the audience of the contrast between&nbsp;
a hero in his physical prime and a hero at 70.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.060 --> 00:09:52.380
We're not relying solely on the audience's&nbsp;
memory of the previous films. It reminds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.380 --> 00:09:56.820
everyone what he's done, what he's survived,&nbsp;
what he's accomplished. By showing him in his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:56.820 --> 00:10:01.740
most hearty and then finding him at 70 in New&nbsp;
York City, it produces for the audience a kind&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.740 --> 00:10:06.435
of wonderful whiplash of how they're going to have&nbsp;
to readjust and retool their brains for this guy."

00:10:06.435 --> 00:10:07.380
"He's about to retire."

00:10:07.380 --> 00:10:08.220
"Yes."

00:10:08.220 --> 00:10:09.960
"From being a professor."

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:10.380
"Yes."

00:10:10.380 --> 00:10:12.510
"And all hell breaks loose."

00:10:12.510 --> 00:10:13.140
"It does."

00:10:13.920 --> 00:10:19.020
This fifth Indiana Jones film has been in&nbsp;
development for a long time. Even all the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:19.020 --> 00:10:23.400
way back in the 1970s, George Lucas and&nbsp;
Steven Spielberg hoped to tell a quintet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.400 --> 00:10:26.820
of stories about the globe-trotting&nbsp;
adventurer. And after having waited&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:26.820 --> 00:10:30.660
so long after The Last Crusade to make&nbsp;
Kingdom of the Crystal Skull, it didn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.660 --> 00:10:34.380
seem like another big-screen outing could ever&nbsp;
happen. But following Crystal Skull's release,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.380 --> 00:10:39.180
Lucas began researching possible story&nbsp;
ideas. As he told the Times Online in 2008,

00:10:39.180 --> 00:10:43.440
"I'm in the future; Steven's in the past. He's&nbsp;
trying to drag it back to the way they were,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:43.440 --> 00:10:47.700
I'm trying to push it to a whole different&nbsp;
place. So, still we have a sort of tension."

00:10:47.700 --> 00:10:52.440
The project was stuck in development for&nbsp;
years before Lucas sold Lucasfilm to Disney,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:52.440 --> 00:10:57.240
who hoped to revive the series without him. At&nbsp;
that point, Spielberg and Crystal Skull writer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.240 --> 00:11:01.140
David Koepp began working on the script for&nbsp;
what would eventually become Dial of Destiny.

00:11:01.140 --> 00:11:06.960
By 2018, Spielberg was preoccupied with other&nbsp;
projects, and Koepp was replaced by Solo writer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:06.960 --> 00:11:12.120
Jonathan Kasdan, son of Raiders of the Lost Ark&nbsp;
scribe Lawrence Kasdan, before returning quickly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.120 --> 00:11:16.980
thereafter. Eventually, Spielberg's version of&nbsp;
Indiana Jones 5 failed because he, Harrison Ford,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:16.980 --> 00:11:21.480
and Disney couldn't all agree on the script.&nbsp;
When James Mangold took the helm, things&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:21.480 --> 00:11:26.520
seemed to be back on track. He rewrote Koepp's&nbsp;
script alongside his Ford v Ferrari writers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:26.520 --> 00:11:31.740
brothers Jez and John-Henry Butterworth, with all&nbsp;
four men receiving final "written by" credits.

00:11:32.520 --> 00:11:37.200
Following the sale of Lucasfilm, George&nbsp;
Lucas distanced himself from both Star Wars&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:37.200 --> 00:11:41.940
and Indiana Jones. After Disney declined to use&nbsp;
his treatments for the Star Wars sequel trilogy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:41.940 --> 00:11:46.860
his involvement in the space opera franchise&nbsp;
has been essentially nonexistent. Besides&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:46.860 --> 00:11:51.000
visiting the set of The Mandalorian, he's&nbsp;
effectively bid his former glories goodbye.

00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:54.780
While Lucas wrote and directed Star&nbsp;
Wars during his time as a filmmaker,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:54.780 --> 00:12:00.240
he was never actually a credited screenwriter for&nbsp;
any Indiana Jones movie. Instead, he helped craft&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:00.240 --> 00:12:04.620
the story for each film, served as a producer,&nbsp;
and worked closely with Spielberg to make sure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:04.620 --> 00:12:08.760
that their shared vision became a reality.&nbsp;
But while Lucas' involvement in the fifth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:08.760 --> 00:12:13.080
Indiana Jones has been diminished following&nbsp;
his sale to Disney, he's still in the loop.

00:12:13.080 --> 00:12:17.520
According to James Mangold, both Spielberg&nbsp;
and Lucas are involved with Dial of Destiny.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:17.520 --> 00:12:21.120
While they may not be in the director's&nbsp;
chair or receiving any story credit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:21.120 --> 00:12:25.020
these two filmmaking giants just had to be&nbsp;
included in another Indiana Jones picture,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:25.020 --> 00:12:29.340
especially if it's going to be the final&nbsp;
one. Serving as executive producers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:29.340 --> 00:12:34.440
Spielberg and Lucas have continued to help curate&nbsp;
Hollywood's most famous archeologist from afar,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:34.440 --> 00:12:39.780
which is surely comforting to plenty of loyal&nbsp;
fans. If they trust Mangold to deliver a killer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:39.780 --> 00:12:43.560
version of Indiana Jones, then the rest&nbsp;
of us probably shouldn't be too worried.

00:12:44.160 --> 00:12:49.380
Since he directed the first four Indiana Jones&nbsp;
movies, one can't help but wonder how Steven&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:49.380 --> 00:12:54.300
Spielberg feels about Dial of Destiny. He's been&nbsp;
the primary creator of the character for decades,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:54.300 --> 00:12:59.007
so an Indiana Jones movie without him&nbsp;
is sort of impossible to even imagine.

00:12:59.400 --> 00:13:00.360
"Oh, dear."

00:13:00.360 --> 00:13:04.980
Of course, the filmmaker is still involved and&nbsp;
serves as an executive producer alongside George&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:04.980 --> 00:13:10.500
Lucas, but he isn't working as closely as he used&nbsp;
to this time around. But regardless of his time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:10.500 --> 00:13:15.120
or lack thereof, on set, Spielberg is still&nbsp;
the authority on all things Indiana Jones,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:15.120 --> 00:13:18.180
which makes his thoughts on Dial&nbsp;
of Destiny all the more exciting.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:18.180 --> 00:13:21.660
After watching the film at a Disney&nbsp;
executive screening, he told Variety,

00:13:21.660 --> 00:13:25.920
"When the lights came up I just turned to&nbsp;
the group and said, 'Damn! I thought I was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:25.920 --> 00:13:29.700
the only one who knew how to make one of these&nbsp;
[...] Everybody loved the movie. It's really,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:29.700 --> 00:13:33.720
really a good Indiana Jones film. I'm really&nbsp;
proud of what [Mangold] has done with it."

00:13:33.720 --> 00:13:37.680
That's high praise coming from the man&nbsp;
who single handedly directed all of this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:37.680 --> 00:13:42.000
character's previous on-screen adventures. With&nbsp;
Spielberg clearly on board with this version,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:44.460
our hopes for Dial of Destiny have only risen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:44.460 --> 00:13:48.949
giving this installment the potential for&nbsp;
this to be one of the best of the series.

00:13:49.200 --> 00:13:53.700
With Indy's favorite Egyptian excavator&nbsp;
Sallah returning for Dial of Destiny,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:53.700 --> 00:13:56.400
many have wondered if other fan&nbsp;
favorites could return as well.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:56.400 --> 00:14:02.250
Among the most requested is Ke Huy Quan's&nbsp;
Short Round from 1984's Temple of Doom.

00:14:02.250 --> 00:14:04.972
"Okee-dokee, Dr. Jones. Hold on to your potatoes!"

00:14:04.972 --> 00:14:09.960
Before recently, Quan was best known for his&nbsp;
work as Short Round and as Data in The Goonies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:09.960 --> 00:14:14.400
which was released the following year. But&nbsp;
then in 2022, he returned to international&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:14.400 --> 00:14:19.920
stardom thanks to the success of the multiversal&nbsp;
action-comedy-drama Everything Everywhere All at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:19.920 --> 00:14:24.240
Once. He played Waymond Wang, which earned&nbsp;
him an Academy Award for Best Supporting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:24.240 --> 00:14:28.740
Actor. After years away from the big screen,&nbsp;
Quan is suddenly doing quite well for himself.

00:14:28.740 --> 00:14:35.400
In 2022, Quan and Harrison Ford shared a tearful&nbsp;
reunion at Disney's D23 convention, but alas, Quan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:35.400 --> 00:14:39.960
has insisted that he isn't returning for Dial of&nbsp;
Destiny. He told Entertainment Tonight in April,

00:14:39.960 --> 00:14:44.520
"I want to say [I'll be in it], but no. Here's the&nbsp;
thing. I don't want to disappoint the fans. I've&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:44.520 --> 00:14:49.200
joked about it all the time, but reuniting with&nbsp;
Harrison after 38 years, that was very special."

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:53.880
With this being Ford's final adventure as Indy,&nbsp;
and Quan unlikely to return as Short Round for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:53.880 --> 00:14:58.380
a potential spinoff, it seems like fans will&nbsp;
just have to settle for the off-screen reunion.

00:14:59.100 --> 00:15:04.200
As Indy's original love interest, Karen Allen's&nbsp;
Marion Ravenwood is the only recurring female&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:04.200 --> 00:15:08.340
character in the Indiana Jones chronology.&nbsp;
First appearing in Raiders of the Lost Ark,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:08.340 --> 00:15:12.300
she and Dr. Jones share a steamy&nbsp;
romantic history. Upon reuniting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:12.300 --> 00:15:14.940
they resume their previous&nbsp;
affairs, at least for a while.

00:15:14.940 --> 00:15:19.080
Since Temple of Doom took place a year&nbsp;
before the events of Raiders and The Last&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:19.080 --> 00:15:23.880
Crusade focused mainly on Indy's relationship&nbsp;
with his father, Marion wasn't in either of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:23.880 --> 00:15:28.260
the first two sequels. But then Kingdom of the&nbsp;
Crystal Skull came along, with Allen appearing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:28.260 --> 00:15:32.820
with their son and managing to finally put a&nbsp;
ring on the elderly archaeologist's finger.

00:15:32.820 --> 00:15:36.540
When Spielberg and Lucas first began&nbsp;
developing the fifth Indiana Jones film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:36.540 --> 00:15:42.000
Allen initially expressed interest in returning&nbsp;
as Marion once more. As she told MovieWeb in 2011,

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:46.140
"I mean, we're married now, so it would be&nbsp;
difficult, I think, to move forward without her."

00:15:46.140 --> 00:15:51.240
But ever since, there's been no official comment&nbsp;
regarding Allen's inclusion in Dial of Destiny.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:51.240 --> 00:15:55.620
Though James Mangold has confirmed that we'll&nbsp;
learn more about what happened to her and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:55.620 --> 00:16:01.440
Indy's son Mutt, we've heard nothing more about&nbsp;
her own status. With Allen seemingly radio silent,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:01.440 --> 00:16:05.651
we can only speculate about whether or not&nbsp;
she'll show up in the final chapter after all.

00:16:05.651 --> 00:16:07.740
"Do you and Harrison talk?&nbsp;
Do you stay in contact?"

00:16:07.740 --> 00:16:09.327
"We talk every now and then."

00:16:09.750 --> 00:16:15.000
For nearly 30 years, the Indiana Jones series was&nbsp;
distributed by the motion picture giant Paramount&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:15.000 --> 00:16:19.800
Pictures after Spielberg and Lucas made a deal for&nbsp;
five Indiana Jones pictures with the distributor.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:19.800 --> 00:16:25.140
The studio's famous mountain logo has appeared&nbsp;
at the beginning of each Indy flick, from 1981's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:25.140 --> 00:16:30.060
Raiders of the Lost Ark all the way to 2008's&nbsp;
Kingdom of the Crystal Skull. It's now pretty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:30.060 --> 00:16:35.040
much synonymous with Harrison Ford's globetrotting&nbsp;
adventures. Alas, nothing in Hollywood lasts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:35.040 --> 00:16:40.680
forever. So after Lucasfilm was sold to the Walt&nbsp;
Disney Company in 2012, Paramount's involvement in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:40.680 --> 00:16:45.600
any future Indiana Jones installments was subject&nbsp;
to change, and that change has in fact happened.

00:16:45.600 --> 00:16:50.220
Paramount has retained its initial distribution&nbsp;
rights for the first four films in the series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:50.220 --> 00:16:53.460
which is why they're currently&nbsp;
available on Paramount+ and not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:53.460 --> 00:16:58.140
Disney+. But the House of Mouse now owns&nbsp;
distribution rights to any future films.

00:16:58.140 --> 00:17:03.060
Dial of Destiny is a co-production between&nbsp;
Lucasfilm and Disney, making it the first Indiana&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:03.060 --> 00:17:08.700
Jones film not solely produced by Lucasfilm. But&nbsp;
Paramount has received an "associate credit" on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:08.700 --> 00:17:13.980
this latest picture, with an undisclosed financial&nbsp;
participation as well. How this all works behind&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:13.980 --> 00:17:17.700
the scenes is a bit of a mystery, but it's&nbsp;
clear that the cooperation between Disney&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:17.700 --> 00:17:22.980
and Paramount has only helped Indiana Jones going&nbsp;
forward. Still, replacing the snow-capped mountain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:22.980 --> 00:17:27.098
with the Disneyland castle will surely be&nbsp;
pretty hard for moviegoers to adjust to.

00:17:27.480 --> 00:17:31.620
Unlike a lot of other action films, the&nbsp;
Indiana Jones series wasn't released in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:31.620 --> 00:17:36.120
strict chronological order. While Dial of&nbsp;
Destiny is the final feature in the saga,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:36.120 --> 00:17:39.480
parts of it fit between some of&nbsp;
Indy's other earlier adventures.

00:17:39.480 --> 00:17:43.260
The first film chronologically in&nbsp;
the Indy timeline is Temple of Doom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:43.260 --> 00:17:48.540
which takes place in 1935. Only a year later,&nbsp;
the events of Raiders of the Lost Ark unfold,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:48.540 --> 00:17:53.040
which see Indy and Marion fight a group of Nazis&nbsp;
in search of the Old Testament relic known as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:53.040 --> 00:17:58.500
the Ark of the Covenant. The Last Crusade&nbsp;
takes place a few years after that in 1939,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:58.500 --> 00:18:03.300
but not before a flashback to Indy's time as&nbsp;
a young man played by River Phoenix set in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:03.300 --> 00:18:08.434
1912. This is as far back in the past that&nbsp;
the feature films have ventured thus far.

00:18:08.434 --> 00:18:10.294
"This should be in a museum."

00:18:10.294 --> 00:18:15.120
Kingdom of the Crystal Skull was released&nbsp;
in 2008, but it takes place in 1957 during&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:15.120 --> 00:18:20.160
the Cold War. A somewhat older Indy finds&nbsp;
his long-lost son Mutt, marries Marion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:20.160 --> 00:18:25.320
and discovers the existence of extraterrestrial,&nbsp;
or rather interdimensional, creatures. As for Dial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:25.320 --> 00:18:30.360
of Destiny, though there will be flashbacks&nbsp;
to 1944, it will reportedly mostly be set in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:30.360 --> 00:18:36.000
1969. Thus, it will be the farthest forward&nbsp;
Indy has ever ventured in the 20th century.

00:18:36.540 --> 00:18:41.460
Described by director James Mangold as "a&nbsp;
hero at sunset," Indy's fifth and final&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:41.460 --> 00:18:45.840
big-screen adventure is set to be his swan&nbsp;
song. And while that's sad on some level,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:45.840 --> 00:18:50.280
there's plenty of mystery and excitement&nbsp;
with such a promise. Mangold is possibly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:50.280 --> 00:18:54.000
best known for directing the final two&nbsp;
installments of Fox's Wolverine trilogy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:54.000 --> 00:18:56.880
so he's no stranger to telling&nbsp;
an action hero's final tale.

00:18:56.880 --> 00:19:02.220
2017's Logan closed the book on Hugh Jackman's&nbsp;
long-running turn as the iconic X-Man,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:02.220 --> 00:19:06.660
at least until Marvel Studios introduced&nbsp;
the idea of him returning again. That film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:06.660 --> 00:19:09.720
pretty much told the definitive&nbsp;
Wolverine story for a generation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:09.720 --> 00:19:13.680
so fans are anxious to see if Dial of&nbsp;
Destiny will employ the same tone and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:13.680 --> 00:19:18.480
effectively serve as Indy's version of Logan. As&nbsp;
Mangold rhetorically asked Entertainment Weekly,

00:19:18.480 --> 00:19:22.920
"What does the hero do when the world no longer&nbsp;
has a place for him? I find it really interesting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:22.920 --> 00:19:27.915
to try to look at classical heroes through the&nbsp;
prism of our jaundiced contemporary attitudes."

00:19:27.915 --> 00:19:33.555
"The best version of this movie was the one that&nbsp;
didn't do everything like all the other movies."&nbsp;

00:19:33.555 --> 00:19:37.980
Mangold also compared Dial of Destiny&nbsp;
to Logan, while reassuring fans that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:37.980 --> 00:19:42.360
the film's tone would remain faithful to&nbsp;
the Indian Jones mythos. He further noted,

00:19:42.360 --> 00:19:46.980
"I am under no illusions that my job making&nbsp;
an Indiana Jones film was to suddenly beat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:46.980 --> 00:19:51.000
the humor out of it and turn it into some&nbsp;
kind of dirge. I think that what we're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:51.000 --> 00:19:55.200
trying to do is balance both an accurate and&nbsp;
realistic appraisal of where this character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:55.200 --> 00:20:00.364
would be at this time in his life, and do that&nbsp;
honestly [...] This is an Indiana Jones film."

00:20:00.480 --> 00:20:05.040
After Disney bought Lucasfilm in 2012,&nbsp;
fans wondered how the House of Mouse would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:05.040 --> 00:20:09.780
continue the Indiana Jones franchise. While&nbsp;
Star Wars has been Disney's main LucasFilm&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:09.780 --> 00:20:13.440
priority following the sale, projects&nbsp;
like Dial of Destiny and the Disney+&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:13.440 --> 00:20:17.700
series Willow prove that there's more to&nbsp;
Lucasfilm's catalog than just Star Wars.

00:20:17.700 --> 00:20:21.540
After Dial of Destiny was greenlit and it&nbsp;
was announced that this would be Harrison&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:21.540 --> 00:20:26.340
Ford's last outing, many speculated that Disney&nbsp;
would attempt to reboot the franchise through a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:26.340 --> 00:20:30.000
series of prequels. And for a while,&nbsp;
that looked like a real possibility.

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:34.560
In 2022, Variety reported that a prequel&nbsp;
series set before the events of Raiders&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:34.560 --> 00:20:39.420
of the Lost Ark and probably Temple of Doom&nbsp;
was in the works at Disney+. But by 2023,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:39.420 --> 00:20:42.720
other sources implied that the series,&nbsp;
which would've been the first Indy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:42.720 --> 00:20:46.500
prequel since The Young Indiana Jones&nbsp;
Chronicles, had been scrapped entirely.

00:20:46.500 --> 00:20:51.360
Then in April, ScreenRant reported that Dial of&nbsp;
Destiny would close out the franchise for good.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:51.360 --> 00:20:56.040
While this news sounds pretty final, recent&nbsp;
years have proven that nothing is permanent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:56.040 --> 00:21:00.480
in Hollywood. And while we shouldn't expect&nbsp;
a reboot any time soon, it would actually be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:00.480 --> 00:21:05.471
surprising if Disney and Lucasfilm never returned&nbsp;
to the world of Indiana Jones ever again.

